.TH ARACNE 1 2000-1月 "aracne" "aracne"
.SH NAME
aracne \- Infer the ARACNE gene regulatory network from the expression matrix.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIaracne(\fBx\fR as <generic> Matrix, 
\fBTF\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBestimator\fR as string = "copula", 
\fBthreshold\fR as string = "permutation", 
\fBmi_cutoff\fR as double = 0, 
\fBquantile\fR as double = 0.95, 
\fBpermutations\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBdpi\fR as string = "auto", 
\fBepsilon\fR as double = 0.1, 
\fBdirection\fR as string = "tf", 
\fBbins\fR as integer = 4, 
\fBmax_neighbors\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmax_genes\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmin_nonzero\fR as double = 0, 
\fBlog2\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBrank\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBstandardize\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBprior\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBprior_min_confidence\fR as double = 0.45, 
\fBprior_factor\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBprior_protection\fR as string = "graded", 
\fBprior_strength\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBprior_tf_augment\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBthreads\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBseed\fR as integer = 1234567, 
\fBverbose\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Infer the ARACNE gene regulatory network from the expression matrix.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- the gene expression matrix, rows are the genes and columns are the samples. 
.PP
.PP
\fBTF\fB \fR\- 
 an optional gene id vector of the transcription factors. When it is given the
 computation space is reduced from \fBN x N\fR to \fBTF x N\fR, and the edges are
 oriented from the TF to the targets; the prior network (the \fBprior\fR argument)
 is additionally used for the threshold relaxation and the DPI protection.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBestimator\fB \fR\- see the \fBaracne_options\fR api; default \fBcopula\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBthreshold\fB \fR\- see the \fBaracne_options\fR api; default \fBpermutation\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmi_cutoff\fB \fR\- the fixed MI threshold, a positive value forces the \fBfixed\fR mode. 
.PP
.PP
\fBquantile\fB \fR\- the quantile of the permutation null distribution, default 0.95. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpermutations\fB \fR\- the number of the gene pairs that are sampled for the null distribution. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdpi\fB \fR\- \fBauto\fR (default), \fBstandard\fR, \fBtf\fR or \fBoff\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBepsilon\fB \fR\- the DPI tolerance, default 0.1. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdirection\fB \fR\- \fBtf\fR (default) or \fBundirected\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBbins\fB \fR\- the bin number of the \fBhistogram\fR estimator, default 4. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_neighbors\fB \fR\- the top-K pruning of each regulator, 0 = no pruning. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_genes\fB \fR\- keep only the top variant genes (the TF genes are always kept). 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_nonzero\fB \fR\- the minimal non-zero ratio of the retained genes. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlog2\fB \fR\- apply \fBlog2(x + 1)\fR before the inference. 
.PP
.PP
\fBrank\fB \fR\- spearman (rank) based copula instead of the pearson one. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstandardize\fB \fR\- z-score the expression vectors before the inference. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior\fB \fR\- 
 the curated \fBTF -> target\fR evidence: the value of the \fBbnlearn::prior_network\fR
 api (a [RegulatoryEdge](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.BioSystem.Core.RegulatoryEdge) vector or pipeline) can be passed directly.
 Only the edges whose confidence reaches **prior_min_confidence**
 are used, and the \fBRegulationType\fR (activator/inhibitor) is exported as the
 \fBregulation\fR column of the edge table.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_min_confidence\fB \fR\- the eligibility threshold of the prior edges, default 0.45. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_factor\fB \fR\- the threshold relaxation factor at the full confidence, default 0.5. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_protection\fB \fR\- \fBgraded\fR (default), \fBsampled\fR or \fBoff\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_strength\fB \fR\- the strength of the graded protection, default 0.5. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_tf_augment\fB \fR\- append the prior regulators into the TF set. 
.PP
.PP
\fBthreads\fB \fR\- the max degree of parallelism, a value that is less than or equals to 0 means "auto". 
.PP
.PP
\fBseed\fB \fR\- the random seed, the result is reproducible for a fixed seed. 
.PP
.PP
\fBverbose\fB \fR\- print the statistics, the top regulons and the top edges. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the fitted [ARACNETools.aracneNetwork()](cref:M:TRNtoolkit.ARACNETools.aracneNetwork(SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.DataFrame.Matrix,System.Object,System.String,System.String,System.Double,System.Double,System.Int32,System.String,System.Double,System.String,System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Double,System.Boolean,System.Boolean,System.Boolean,System.Object,System.Double,System.Double,System.String,System.Double,System.Boolean,System.Int32,System.Int32,System.Boolean,SMRUCC.Rsharp.Runtime.Environment)) object. Use the \fBedges\fR/\fBregulons\fR/
 \fBsummary\fR/\fBas_graph\fR api to inspect it, and the \fBwrite_edges\fR api to export it.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let net = ARACNE::aracne(hsa, TF = TF$Symbol, prior = prior, prior_protection = "graded");
 let tab = ARACNE::edges(net);
 write.csv(ARACNE::edges(net), file = "./aracne-edges.csv");
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
ARACNE
